| `scripts/shell_gate.py` | The shell scripts' one adapter, and the one definition of a shell file: `kind` says whether a file is a shell script or a shell test by its suffix or its shebang, and `excluded_by` names the `shell.excluded_paths` entry that covers a path, so `scripts/check_structure.py` holds the same files to the header rule that the shell tools judge. | `make lint-sh`, `make fmt-check-sh`, `make test-sh`; imported by check_O and check_V | [`shell.excluded_paths`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.script_suffixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.shebang_shells`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.test_suffixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | `classify` lists what git could commit, and check_O walks the code roots, so a shell file outside them meets the tools and not the header rule. The make-target rows above carry the tool modes. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
